    "nodes": [
      {
        "id": "note-anthropic",
        "name": "Note - Why /v1/models",
        "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
        "typeVersion": 1,
        "position": [
          -40,
          60
        ],
        "parameters": {
          "width": 460,
          "height": 200,
          "content": "## Anthropic check uses GET /v1/models\n\nDeliberate: it authenticates the API key without generating any tokens.\n\nA Messages call would bill on every health check — and Case 2's budget is $0 additional (CLAUDE.md). A health endpoint that costs money per poll is a health endpoint nobody polls."
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "note-degraded",
        "name": "Note - Degraded not failed",
        "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
        "typeVersion": 1,
        "position": [
          900,
          60
        ],
        "parameters": {
          "width": 460,
          "height": 200,
          "content": "## One dead service = degraded, not crashed\n\nEvery check runs Continue-On-Fail with timeout 10s + 1 retry, so a single unreachable service still returns a readable report naming which one is down.\n\nIf the whole workflow crashed instead, the operator would learn nothing except 'it broke'."
        }
      },
